# The name of the extension in Settings and the store
extension-name = Tailor
extension-description = Dresses other apps in Luft's look, following the desktop's colors, fonts and light and dark styles
found = Apps found on this computer
nothing-found = None of the apps Tailor can dress are on this computer.
try-again = Try again
stopped = Tailor stopped unexpectedly, so this app isn't following the desktop right now.
spotify = Spotify
    .description = Takes on Luft's look through Spicetify, and follows the desktop while it's open.
spotify-no-spicetify = Spicetify isn't installed. Get it from spicetify.app first.
spotify-no-spotify = Spicetify can't find Spotify. Open Spotify once, then try again.
spotify-no-prefs = Spicetify needs Spotify to have been opened once. Open Spotify, sign in, close it, then try again.
spotify-read-only = This Spotify is installed for everyone, so its files can't be changed. Install Spotify from Schelf for your account only, then try again.
spotify-for-you = Spotify for your account only
open-schelf = Open Schelf
spotify-not-stock = Spicetify's backup doesn't match this Spotify, and its original files are gone. Reinstall Spotify, which keeps your account and settings, then try again.
spotify-too-new = This Spotify is newer than your Spicetify. Update Spicetify, then try again.
spotify-working = Putting the theme in place
spotify-failed = Spicetify couldn't dress Spotify. Updating Spicetify often helps.
spotify-restart = Restart Spotify to see its new look.
spotify-ready = Spotify follows the desktop whenever it's open. If it's open and hasn't changed, restart it.
spotify-connected = Spotify is following the desktop.
steam = Steam
    .description = Its library, menus and windows take on Luft's look, even after Steam updates. Store pages stay as they are.
steam-first-run = Open Steam once so it can finish installing, then try again.
steam-failed = Steam couldn't be dressed. Check that Steam is up to date, then try again.
steam-ready = Steam picks up the desktop's look each time it opens. It can't change while it's open.
vesktop = Vesktop
    .description = A theme in Luft's look that follows the desktop. Vesktop runs Vencord, which Discord doesn't allow; Tailor only adds the theme.
vesktop-first-run = Open Vesktop once, change any setting so it saves them, then try again.
vesktop-failed = Vesktop couldn't be dressed. Check that it's up to date, then try again.
vesktop-quit-once = Quit Vesktop once, from its tray icon too, so the theme can be turned on.
vesktop-ready = Vesktop follows the desktop whenever it's open.
